# online podcast search

Source `src\utilities.ps1`, then use `$pods = invoke_podcasts -Query "software; $pods.podcasts | Select-Object -Property title, description"`.

# local podcast search

found within `src\setup.ps1`, the function returns `(Get-Content $PODCASTS_FILEPATH -ErrorAction Stop) | ConvertFrom-Json -Depth 6`
* `$PODCASTS_FILEPATH` set by joining `$PSScriptRoot` and `$PODCASTS_BASENAME`. 
* `$PODCASTS_BASENAME` is just `podcasts`; `src\setup.ps1` L45; <!-- ?!? THIS IS AN AUTOMATIC RESOURCE BUT IS PLACED IN THE SRC FOLDER -->

# saving the podcast file

The function `save_podcasts` of `src\setup.ps1` saves the provided podcast information as JSON.

